  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>ksdensity</keyword>
  <short_description>Kernel smoothing function estimate.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>[f, xi] = ksdensity(x)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[f, xi] = ksdensity(x, pts)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[f, xi, bw] = ksdensity(...)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[...] = ksdensity(..., Name, Value)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>ksdensity(...)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>ksdensity</b> estimates a smoothed distribution function from univariate sample data using a normal kernel.</p>
    <p>Name-value arguments include Bandwidth, Width, Function, NumPoints, Support, Weights, Frequency, Censoring, Kernel, and BoundaryCorrection. Supported function types are pdf, cdf, survivor, cumhazard, and icdf.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[x = [0 1 2];
[f, xi, bw] = ksdensity(x)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
